This page contains a list of things that could be done to improve this project.

If someone is interested in participating in one of these tasks, don't hesitate to contact me or to open a Pull Request

FFT
###

The FFT implementation is fairly good, yet several things could be improved

* A 6-point transform module could be added to improve performance further
* There is still room for improvement in some transform modules
* The Inverse FFT implementation should not make multiple pass over the data, this mean that the conjugate should be done directly inside the transform modules based on a function parameter
* Add support for ifft_many (and 2d)

GPU
###

The GPU support is quite small for now (FFT and GEMM), other routines could be faster using GPU, especially convolutions and maybe pooling.

Matrix Multiplication
#####################

1. An efficient implementation for floats and complex numbers would greatly benefit the library.
2. An AVX-optimized matrix multiplication algorithm for double would be of great value
3. Improving the standard multiplication algorithm for complex numbers would be a great improvement as well.

Misc
####

1. Reduce the compile-time overhead of the library expressions
2. Fix the exponential template instantiation issue of the optimizer
3. Improve performance of out of place matrix transposition
